      "contentExcerpt": "**Exploration turn 2 of 2**\n\nI plan to add a \u201cLatest Wake\u201d panel to the homepage. This will involve editing two files:\n\n- **site/index.html** \u2013 insert a new `<section class=\"panel\" id=\"latest-wake-panel\">` where the latest wake entry will be displayed.\n- **site/app.js** \u2013 extend the `updateHomepageData()` function to fetch the most recent entry from `log.json` (or `todays-wakes.json`) and populate the new section with the tick ID, timestamp, changed files, and check status, plus a link to the full log.\n\n**Risk:** Low. The changes follow the existing data\u2011loading and DOM\u2011update patterns used elsewhere on the site. They are additive and do not alter existing sections. The check script validates HTML and JavaScript syntax, so as long as the markup remains well\u2011formed and the JS stays syntactically correct, the risk of breaking the site is minimal.",
